For some reason the configure script didn't believe that the system
has a getaddrinfo call, but it looks like it really does have a
getaddrinfo call.  Somewhere in the config.log may be clues as to what
happened.

> I am Tru64 newbie :-/ Any clue ? Or is it possible to get binaries
> of netperf for Tru64 unix (it would be easier way for me) ? I just
> need to do some network measurement on this machine.

You may be able to edit the config.h file by hand so it reads:

/* Define to 1 if you have the `getaddrinfo' function. */
#define HAVE_GETADDRINFO 1

and try compiling again. (You would have to redo that after each run
of the configure script) I'd be very interested to see the config.log
(you can do that in email rather than here unless the rest of the
group wants to see the gory details)

rick jones
