Halt the system and power it off. Unplug the power supply cables one at
a time from the back of the machine and wait for the PS light on the
back of each one to go off (capacitor discharged). The fan controller
stores the error as long as power is applied to the computer since
normally there's no battery on this controller. Doing this should take
care of the fail flag.

Plug the power supply cables back in and powerup as normal. Voila! That
should be it. If you happen to have a battery on the fan control NVRAM,
you could pop it out if the above procedure doesn't work for you. You
won't hurt anything doing this.

Jack

