Wim Cossement wrote:
> 
> Since I'm a bit of a n00b with Tru64 (can't say I like it either ;-)

You should bite your tongue when asking for help :)

> was wondering if anyone could tell me why I get all those different 
> hidden files in some dirs, especially /etc.
> 
> .mrg..inetd.conf
> .new..inetd.conf
> .proto..inetd.conf
> 
> So what are al those things anyway?

These files are used during installs, update installs, and patch 
application to create and merge-in changes to system files.  The .mrg..* 
files are actually merge scripts, the others are used during the 
process, along with the 'real' file (it's actually more complicated than 
that, but you get the picture).

> Some sort of backup? If it is, I think it's rather messy.
> They differ with the 'real' version, and most files are not the same 
> amongst .new, .mrg and .proto either.
> 
> Can they safely be deleted or moved to another location?

Not if you ever want to install patches, etc.  They're also good for 
restoring trashed system files that have not been backed-up.

-Brian


